  "ruling": {
    "body": "**Architect (Sol), 2026-10-01: rulings on quest data (5933181185) and Wheel/Gem values (#1456, 5932656862).** No owner gate and no new contract; the closed vocabularies are unchanged.\n\n**1. Quest data (D277)**\n\n| Case | Ruling |\n|---|---|\n| Container chests (a filled container) | **Covered.** BAGS-0 (containers with contents) is the nested-bags decision that the reward-chest slice \u00a75.1 waited on. A contents field in the quest reward schema is a content-lane child after close-out. Until then, these rows stay `waiting_data`. |\n| Key chests | **Covered.** Quest format \u00a73/\u00a73.1 `reward.key_binding` (`\u2026:door-key/<n>`) and DUR-03 \u00a739.3. Author them now. |\n| Text chests (book or letter) | **Covered.** Quest format \u00a73 `reward.written_text` and WRITE-0 (merged). Author them now. |\n| Random chests | **Covered.** Quest format \u00a73 `reward.random_one_of` and QUEST-STATE-0 \u00a78 (CHEST-RANDOM-1). Author them now. |\n| Cooldown chests | **Covered.** Quest format `repeat: cooldown(hours)`, with identity per reward-chest \u00a75.1 (claim, character, cycle ordinal). Author the data now; the runtime is a later child. |\n| Achievement chests | **New architecture item after close-out** (an Achievement owner, per reward-chest \u00a76). Author the typed grant reference; the claim records the grant request. Runtime admission waits for that item. |\n| Item 3081 (charged amulet) | **Covered.** The reward is **one** ItemInstance with count 1. Its 5 charges come from the Item definition's `charges.count` (item schema; EQUIP-0 \u00a73.1), never from the reward line. Add the charges fact from TibiaWiki first. The charge behaviour itself waits for TIMED-ITEM-0 (EQUIP-0: `timed` items grant nothing until then). |\n| Conditions or effects outside the closed vocabulary | **Stay `unresolved`/`waiting_data`.** Group them by kind in the closeout packet. Each new kind is a new architecture item after close-out. Do not widen the vocabulary in data. |\n\nIntegrating this owner-directed continuation into the D252 close-out schedule is the control plane's call.\n\n**2. Wheel/Gem (#1456).** All five values are ruleset data, not owner decisions. 250 and 12M were Canary values marked PARITY_PENDING in WHEEL-GEM-0 \u00a72/\u00a75.1. The FORMULA rule settles them, in this order: official statement, then English TibiaWiki, then Canary as the fallback. A conflict that remains is PARITY_PENDING and stays unadmitted at runtime.\n\n| Item | Ruling |\n|---|---|\n| Revealed-gem cap 250 vs 225 | **225** (TibiaWiki) unless an official statement says otherwise; record Canary's 250 as conflict evidence. |\n| Supreme Grade III 12M vs 12.5M | **12.5M** (TibiaWiki); record Canary's 12M as conflict evidence. |\n| Mystic Repulse II +40% / +15% (BR) / +60% (planner) | Use English TibiaWiki's value if it gives one, otherwise Canary's. The BR wiki and the planner are corroboration only. The Sept 27 +40% stays only if one of those two sources supports it; otherwise it is **PARITY_PENDING**. |\n| Guiding Presence Q5 (relative vs points, rounding, monk's own copy) | Canary's arithmetic decides where TibiaWiki is silent. If Canary does not implement it, it is **PARITY_PENDING** with no runtime admission. No owner gate. |\n| Task Shop +50 / Grade IV max 69 | **OUT_OF_SCOPE** for now. These belong to systems that are not admitted, so they stay recorded as references only and no value is accepted. |\n\nMitigation wording, runtime effect and asset admission, and paid-gem execution stay in the GEM-R/DUR-02 scope. Nothing here goes to the owner.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
